A compact way to write the mechanism is $\begin{aligned}
\hbox{idea only}
&\longrightarrow
\hbox{high investor uncertainty},
\\
\hbox{demonstrable artifact}
&\longrightarrow
\hbox{lower investor uncertainty},
\\
\hbox{real user acceptance}
&\longrightarrow
\hbox{stronger market proof}.\end{aligned}$ The negative version is just as important: $\hbox{flashy presentation} \not\equiv \hbox{validated demand}.$

